Fix: Scanning a deck-share QR code now actually imports the deck instead of always failing.
Change: Importing a deck via QR code or file/JSON now opens the create-deck screen pre-filled with the deck's values instead of importing it directly.
Fix: Scanning a QR code now shows a loading indicator right away, so the app no longer looks frozen while it's processing.
New: Species database updates now always ask for confirmation before installing, on Wi-Fi or cellular alike, instead of installing silently over Wi-Fi.
Change: After importing a deck, you can now choose to download base data only, full data (including iNaturalist), or no data at all, instead of base data starting automatically.
Fix: In Edit Deck, the button for a deck with no downloaded data now reopens the data-choice dialog again, instead of incorrectly starting only iNaturalist enrichment.
New: After a species database update, you're now asked whether to refresh already-downloaded base images; you can also do this later, per deck, from "Edit Deck".
Fix: Edit Deck's "Enrich again" button now always reopens the data-choice dialog instead of jumping straight to a full iNaturalist pass, and now reliably fetches additional iNaturalist photos even when base data already finished earlier.
Fix: Re-enriching now actually re-checks base images against the local image cache, instead of silently doing nothing for an already-finished deck.
Change: When photos or data are missing during review, the app now directly offers the right download or enrichment.
New: Wrong answer options in multiple-choice review mode are now drawn from the same genus/family/order as the species being asked about, instead of completely at random from the whole deck.
New: The watchlist button is now also available on the back of the flashcard, so you can add a species to your watchlist even after flipping it.
New: In multiple-choice review mode, you can flip the card again after the answer is revealed to look at the image once more — your answer can no longer be changed.
New: On the flashcard back, you can now switch languages on the spot to check a species' name in another language, without changing your deck settings.
